{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1330171-enhancement-cap","id":1330171,"title":"Enhancement cap?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-09T17:03:39-07:00","id":1330171,"title":"Enhancement cap?","content":"Does Scion have an enhancement limit? I found 1 reference to a limit but it says \u201cas mentioned previously\u201d (p105) and I can\u2019t find the previous mention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T17:39:12-07:00","id":1330174,"title":"","content":"3 is the soft cap.<br /> Essentially what you could get without &quot;magic&quot;<br /> <br /> 5 is the hard cap. Usually explain by adding some magical sdvantages.<br /> <br /> And then you can always add on top the scale enhancement bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T19:56:36-07:00","id":1330194,"title":"","content":"Please direct me to where I can read that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T20:20:16-07:00","id":1330198,"title":"","content":"The line that you cited as reiterating the cap also reiterates the cap. It gives you the hard limit.<br /> <br /> Also, the free Errata/FAQ document on DriveThru goes into more detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FAQ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is not mentioned under the Storypath rules section, page 105 of Scion: Origin clarifies that Enhancement cannot stack above 5, from either a single source or multiple sources. However, Storyguides are heavily encouraged to be judicious in allowing Enhancements greater than 3 at any one time from multiple sources. One can only have so many blessings, headwinds, and good fortune at any one time before it becomes superfluous. Scale explicitly allows for Enhancement above 5, as an exception. If Zeus punches you, you\u2019re going to feel it</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[